==English==

===Adverb===
{{infl|en|adverb|head=[[in]] [[the]] [[long run]]}}

# {{idiomatic}} After a very long time; [[eventually]]; over a long period of time; more generally.
#* '''1923''', [[w:John Maynard Keynes|John Maynard Keynes]], ''A Tract on Monetary Reform'', ch. 3:
#*: '''In the long run''' we are all dead.
#* '''1951''', [[w:Arthur C. Clarke|Arthur C. Clarke]], ''The Exploration of Space'', p. 111:
#*: If we have learned one thing from the history of invention and discovery, it is that, '''in the long run''' — and often in the short one — the most daring prophecies seem laughably conservative.

====Synonyms====
* [[in the long term]]

